| dockerix: RISC OS boot script, served from the container via Arculator's
| HostFS. RISC OS runs it at every start (CMOS: FileSystem HostFS, Boot).
| It is idempotent and builds the rest of the CMOS configuration itself:
| on a clean CMOS the RMLoad only loads RISCiXFS (the Device/Unit/Partition
| options exist only once it is loaded), the Configure lines set the SCSI
| root and the NoRISCOS autoboot flag, and re-initialising RISCiXFS makes
| it read them and boot the kernel. On every later start NoRISCOS is already
| set, so RISCiXFS boots RISC iX as soon as it is loaded and nothing after
| the RMLoad runs.
Echo dockerix: !Boot running from HostFS
Configure NoCaps
Configure MonitorType 1
| SCSIFSdiscs is read when SCSIFS initialises, so re-init it to pick the
| change up on a first run (on a clean CMOS there are no SCSI discs yet).
Configure SCSIFSdiscs 1
RMReInit SCSIFS
RMLoad SCSI::4.$.!RISCiX.RISCiXFS
Configure Device sd0
Configure Unit 0
Configure Partition 0
Configure NoRISCOS
RMReInit RISCiXFS
